I recommend “International Forum”, it's a space where Mexicans go to meet internationals, and internationals go to meet Mexicans. For some reason, most international students are not interested, so it ends up being a bunch of Mexican students and a few internationals. I liked this a lot, as there's no real structure, and the few times I was there, I just talked to other Mexicans and asked questions about food, culture, whatever I wanted to basically. They were also really eager to share. I also got in the Whatsapp group, and one time I needed a charger for example, so I asked in the group if anyone was at campus and ended up spending the afternoon with two Mexican students, while I used their charger to charge my phone. That was great, without the club/whatsapp group I would've never met them. The club kinda got boring after a while though, I think the organizers were afraid of not having structured activities, so they made us play games a lot, whereas I would have rather just had time to talk, so I stopped coming, but I ofc stayed in the Whatsapp group, and met other people through there as well. Any other club you feel would be interesting to you as well, join! If you don't like it, you're not obligated to continue. Paid activities --> (
https://talleres.udlap.mx/
). Academic clubs --> (
https://www.udlap.mx/web/vidaestudiantil/organizacionesestudiantiles.aspx
) scroll down to find the clubs, or visit their facebook page (
https://www.facebook.com/organizaciones.estudiantilesudlap
)
